				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.186
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1298
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. χάρις</span>”
				<i>as of roses,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					5.80
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Dionys.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLit.Lond.</u>
				99.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ῥοδόεντι Λυκόρμᾳ</span> on the
				<i>rose-clad</i> banks of L., <i><span class="en">
				B.
				15.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>rosecoloured</i>, 
